/-!
# The integral `p`-adic `GL_n` Hecke ring comparison

For a prime `p`, let `pLocalSubring n p` (`R_p`) be Shimura's `p`-local subring of
`IntegralHeckeRing n = 𝕋 (posDetInt n) (SLnZ n) ℤ`, generated by the monotone `p`-power diagonal
double cosets `T(p ^ e₁, …, p ^ eₙ)`, and let `PadicIntegralHeckeRing n p` be the integral `p`-adic
Hecke ring `𝕋 (padicIntEntries (Fin n) p) (GLPadicInt (Fin n) p) ℤ` of
`(GL_n(ℤ_p), M_n(ℤ_p) ∩ GL_n(ℚ_p))`.

The purely global rational-matrix objects (`pPrimaryPosDetInt`, `pLocalPosGL`, and
`pPrimaryToPLocalRingEquiv : 𝕋 (pPrimaryPosDetInt n p) (SLnZ n) ℤ ≃+* pLocalSubring n p`) live in
`TauCeti.NumberTheory.HeckeRing.GLn.PPrimary`. Following Rhodes–Shemanske (1998, §3.1 Proposition
3.2 and §3.2 Lemma 3.3) together with Theorem 3.20 of [Shimura][shimura1971], this file proves the
integral `p`-adic comparison `pLocalSubring n p ≃+* PadicIntegralHeckeRing n p`, preserving `1`,
`*`, double-coset degrees `HeckeCoset.degree`, and the degree homomorphism `LeftCosetModule.deg`:

1. **Transversal and stabilizer matching via sublattice completion**: using
   `TauCeti.exists_det_eq_pow_and_mul_eq_map` from `TauCeti.NumberTheory.Padics.FiniteSublattice`
   (every nonsingular `B ∈ M_n(ℤ_p)` agrees up to right multiplication by `GL_n(ℤ_p)` with an
   integer matrix whose determinant is a power `p ^ m`), every left coset of `GL_n(ℤ_p)` in
   `padicIntEntries (Fin n) p` meets the image of `pPrimaryPosDetInt n p`
   (`exists_mem_GLPadicInt_mul_mem_map_pPrimaryPosDetInt`), and `SL_n(ℤ)` acts transitively on the
   stabilizer quotients (`exists_mem_map_SLnZ_inv_mul_mem_conj_GLPadicInt`).
2. **Group-level Hecke comparison**: transporting `(pPrimaryPosDetInt n p, SLnZ n)` along the
   injective embedding `castGLPadic (Fin n) p : GL_n(ℚ) →* GL_n(ℚ_p)` and extending along the
   subgroup intersection `(SLnZ n).map (castGLPadic (Fin n) p) = GLPadicInt (Fin n) p ⊓
   (pLocalPosGL n p).map (castGLPadic (Fin n) p)` via `DoubleCoset.multiplicity_eq_of_inf` and
   `HeckeCosetModule.mapSubgroupRingEquiv` gives `pPrimaryToPadicIntegralRingEquiv :
   𝕋 (pPrimaryPosDetInt n p) (SLnZ n) R ≃+* 𝕋 (padicIntEntries (Fin n) p) (GLPadicInt (Fin n) p) R`
   over any coefficient semiring `R`.
3. **Comparison with `pLocalSubring` and polynomial presentation**: composing with
   `pPrimaryToPLocalRingEquiv` yields
   `pLocalToPadicIntegralRingEquiv : pLocalSubring n p ≃+* PadicIntegralHeckeRing n p` and
   `padicPolynomialRingEquiv : MvPolynomial (Fin n) ℤ ≃+* PadicIntegralHeckeRing n p`, together
   with `degree_padicNatPowDiagCoset_const` (`deg(pI) = 1`). Rank-`2` degree specializations live in
   `TauCeti/NumberTheory/HeckeRing/GL2/Padic.lean`.

## Main definitions

* `HeckeRing.GLn.pPrimaryToPadicIntegralCosetEquiv`: double-coset bijection between
  `(pPrimaryPosDetInt n p, SLnZ n)` and `(padicIntEntries (Fin n) p, GLPadicInt (Fin n) p)`.
* `HeckeRing.GLn.pPrimaryToPadicIntegralRingEquiv`, `HeckeRing.GLn.pLocalToPadicIntegralRingEquiv`,
  `HeckeRing.GLn.padicPolynomialRingEquiv`: the integral `p`-adic comparison isomorphisms and
  polynomial presentation.

## References

* J. A. Rhodes and T. R. Shemanske, *Bruhat–Tits buildings and Hecke operators*, 12 June 1998
  author manuscript, §3.1 Proposition 3.2 and §3.2 Lemma 3.3.
* [J. A. Rhodes and T. R. Shemanske,
  *Rationality theorems for Hecke operators on GL_n*][rhodes1999], §2.
* [G. Shimura, *Introduction to the arithmetic theory of automorphic functions*][shimura1971],
  §3.2, Theorem 3.20.
-/

public section

open Matrix Subgroup Subgroup.Commensurable DoubleCoset TauCeti
